  "summary_en": "Egypt's 2023 voluntary charter for responsible AI, issued by the National Council for AI. It localises OECD, UNESCO and other guidelines into general and implementation guidelines covering fairness, transparency, accountability, human oversight, and risk management. It rejects AI legal personality. Military AI and embodied systems get only passing mention.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Users have a right to know when interacting with an AI rather than a human.",
   "AI systems must not be given legal personality; accountability rests with natural or legal persons.",
   "Final human determination must always be in place, with the ability to modify, stop or retire the system.",
   "Sector regulators should introduce certification mechanisms for AI safety, robustness and reliability.",
   "Developers must adopt systematic risk management; government AI projects are supervised by MCIT and reported to NCAI."
  ],
